      "description": "Watch Bromley vs AFC Wimbledon highlights and goals from League One on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 7, 2026. The stage was set for a compelling League One encounter as Bromley hosted AFC Wimbledon . Both sets of supporters were in high spirits, anticipating a match filled with tactical battles and high-octane football under the floodlights. Early Breakthrough and Tactical Upheaval The match, held on 2026-09-07, exploded into life just eight minutes in. James Tilley turned provider with a pinpoint delivery that found Jayden Stockley , who clinically dispatched his effort to give AFC Wimbledon an early lead. The visitors looked dominant, but their momentum was soon tested by a series of unexpected events as the half progressed. In a bizarre turn of events around the 28-minute mark, Wimbledon were forced into a massive triple substitution. James Tilley , goalkeeper Shamal George , and Deon Woodman all had to leave the field, replaced by Callum Maycock , Owen Mason , and Kamarl Grant . Despite the disruption, the visitors held their nerve, even as Dan Sweeney picked up a yellow card just before the interval, heading into the break with their lead intact. Hippolyte Seals the Points As the second half commenced, Bromley attempted to fight their way back into the contest, introducing Mickel Miller and Victor Adeboyejo to spark their attack. However, it was AFC Wimbledon who struck the decisive blow in the 67th minute. Jayden Stockley turned from scorer to creator, teeing up Myles Hippolyte , who finished with aplomb to double the advantage and put the visitors in a commanding position. In the closing stages, Bromley ’s frustrations grew, evidenced by a yellow card for substitute John McKiernan . Wimbledon managed the game professionally, utilizing their bench to introduce fresh legs like Andy Yiadom and Zack Nelson to see out the contest. After eight minutes of stoppage time, the final whistle confirmed a resilient and clinical victory for the away side."
